<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">

  <!-- Header -->
  <div class="mb-8">
    <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-semibold text-slate-900 leading-tight mb-2">Support</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated: <%= updatedDate %></p>
    <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mt-4">Thank you for using <strong class="font-semibold text-slate-900"><%= siteName %></strong>. The FAQ below can resolve most issues instantly; if your problem persists, choose the contact channel that matches the type of issue.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-3">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
  <div class="divide-y divide-slate-200 border-y border-slate-200 mb-10">

    <details class="group">
      <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 py-4 cursor-pointer select-none list-none font-medium text-slate-800 group-hover:text-brand-700">
        <span>Can't log in / forgot password</span>
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-slate-400 shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M5.23 7.21a.75.75 0 011.06.02L10 11.17l3.71-3.94a.75.75 0 111.08 1.04l-4.25 4.5a.75.75 0 01-1.08 0l-4.25-4.5a.75.75 0 01.02-1.06z" clip-rule="evenodd"/></svg>
      </summary>
      <div class="pb-5 text-sm text-slate-600">
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>Click "Forgot password" at the bottom of the login page and follow the link in your email to reset it.</li>
          <li>If you enabled MFA but can't find your authenticator: log in using the backup codes you downloaded when setting up MFA, then immediately disable and re-enable MFA.</li>
          <li>If the email doesn't arrive: first check your spam folder; if it's still missing, contact the site operator to resend it.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="group">
      <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 py-4 cursor-pointer select-none list-none font-medium text-slate-800 group-hover:text-brand-700">
        <span>App QR login fails / keeps spinning</span>
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-slate-400 shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M5.23 7.21a.75.75 0 011.06.02L10 11.17l3.71-3.94a.75.75 0 111.08 1.04l-4.25 4.5a.75.75 0 01-1.08 0l-4.25-4.5a.75.75 0 01.02-1.06z" clip-rule="evenodd"/></svg>
      </summary>
      <div class="pb-5 text-sm text-slate-600">
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>Confirm your phone can open the <code class="text-[0.85em] bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded"><%= siteName %></code> website normally (i.e. your phone can reach the server).</li>
          <li>Go to "Settings → My Devices → Bind New Device" to generate a fresh QR code and try again (old codes expire after 10 minutes).</li>
          <li>Accounts with MFA enabled must use the "QR login" flow and cannot use the "email + password" quick login.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="group">
      <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 py-4 cursor-pointer select-none list-none font-medium text-slate-800 group-hover:text-brand-700">
        <span>Events not syncing / missing from week view</span>
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-slate-400 shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M5.23 7.21a.75.75 0 011.06.02L10 11.17l3.71-3.94a.75.75 0 111.08 1.04l-4.25 4.5a.75.75 0 01-1.08 0l-4.25-4.5a.75.75 0 01.02-1.06z" clip-rule="evenodd"/></svg>
      </summary>
      <div class="pb-5 text-sm text-slate-600">
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>Pull down on the calendar list in the app to trigger a pull-to-refresh.</li>
          <li>Quit the app and reopen it; it automatically re-fetches the latest events on foreground startup.</li>
          <li>Confirm the event's calendar hasn't been hidden under "Settings → Filter Calendars".</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="group">
      <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 py-4 cursor-pointer select-none list-none font-medium text-slate-800 group-hover:text-brand-700">
        <span>How to invite others to an event</span>
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-slate-400 shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M5.23 7.21a.75.75 0 011.06.02L10 11.17l3.71-3.94a.75.75 0 111.08 1.04l-4.25 4.5a.75.75 0 01-1.08 0l-4.25-4.5a.75.75 0 01.02-1.06z" clip-rule="evenodd"/></svg>
      </summary>
      <div class="pb-5 text-sm text-slate-600">
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>Web / iOS: edit the event → "Manage Participants" → enter the person's email → send (on iOS this is only available for already-saved events).</li>
          <li>They receive an invitation email with an .ics attachment, and after they reply with their RSVP you can see the accepted/declined status in the event details.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="group">
      <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 py-4 cursor-pointer select-none list-none font-medium text-slate-800 group-hover:text-brand-700">
        <span>Subscribing in Apple Calendar / Outlook</span>
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-slate-400 shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M5.23 7.21a.75.75 0 011.06.02L10 11.17l3.71-3.94a.75.75 0 111.08 1.04l-4.25 4.5a.75.75 0 01-1.08 0l-4.25-4.5a.75.75 0 01.02-1.06z" clip-rule="evenodd"/></svg>
      </summary>
      <div class="pb-5 text-sm text-slate-600">
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>Read-only subscription: on the web, right-click the calendar → "Subscription Link" to generate an ICS address → in Apple Calendar, "File → New Calendar Subscription" and paste it.</li>
          <li>Two-way sync: use CalDAV, with a dedicated username/password generated under "Settings → Application Passwords".</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </details>

        <details id="api-token" class="group">
      <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 py-4 cursor-pointer select-none list-none font-medium text-slate-800 group-hover:text-brand-700">
        <span>API tokens &amp; third-party tools</span>
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-slate-400 shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M5.23 7.21a.75.75 0 011.06.02L10 11.17l3.71-3.94a.75.75 0 111.08 1.04l-4.25 4.5a.75.75 0 01-1.08 0l-4.25-4.5a.75.75 0 01.02-1.06z" clip-rule="evenodd"/></svg>
      </summary>
      <div class="pb-5 text-sm text-slate-600">
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>Create one yourself under Settings → Devices → API tokens. Choose read-only unless the tool needs to write — the full token is shown only once, so copy it straight into the tool.</li>
          <li>Got a 401? Check in this order: (1) the site operator hasn't enabled the API — only the operator can change that; (2) the token was revoked or has expired — check the same settings page and create a new one; (3) the account was suspended — that's the operator too.</li>
          <li>Revoking takes effect immediately. Remember to update the token in n8n, Zapier or your scripts afterwards, or they'll keep failing with the old one.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details id="api-usage" class="group">
      <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 py-4 cursor-pointer select-none list-none font-medium text-slate-800 group-hover:text-brand-700">
        <span>Access my calendars via the API (scripts / automation)</span>
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-slate-400 shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M5.23 7.21a.75.75 0 011.06.02L10 11.17l3.71-3.94a.75.75 0 111.08 1.04l-4.25 4.5a.75.75 0 01-1.08 0l-4.25-4.5a.75.75 0 01.02-1.06z" clip-rule="evenodd"/></svg>
      </summary>
      <div class="pb-5 text-sm text-slate-600">
        <p class="mb-3">Once you have a token, any tool that can make HTTPS requests (scripts, n8n, Zapier, Shortcuts…) can read and write your own calendars with it. This is the minimal guide; the full machine-readable spec is <a class="text-brand-700 hover:underline" href="<%= baseUrl %>/api/v1/openapi.json">openapi.json</a> — import it into Postman or a similar tool to generate client code.</p>
        <p class="font-medium text-slate-800 mb-1.5">Authentication & base URL</p>
        <p class="mb-3">Send the header <code class="text-[0.85em] bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Authorization: Bearer <redacted></code> with every request. The base URL is <code class="text-[0.85em] bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded"><%= baseUrl %>/api/v1</code>. Every /api/v1 response is wrapped: success is {"ok": true, "data": …}, failure is {"ok": false, "error": {"code": "…", "message": "…"}}.</p>
        <p class="font-medium text-slate-800 mb-1.5">Common endpoints</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 mb-3">
          <li><code class="text-[0.85em] bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">GET /calendars</code> — list my calendars</li>
          <li><code class="text-[0.85em] bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">POST /calendars</code> — create a calendar (write token)</li>
          <li><code class="text-[0.85em] bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">PATCH /calendars/{id} · DELETE /calendars/{id}</code> — update / delete a calendar (write token)</li>
          <li><code class="text-[0.85em] bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">GET /events?from=…&amp;to=…</code> — list events in a time window (from and to are required, ISO times with offset; calendarIds optional, comma-separated)</li>
          <li><code class="text-[0.85em] bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">GET /calendars/{id}/events</code> — events of one calendar</li>
          <li><code class="text-[0.85em] bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">GET /events/{id}</code> — one event in full</li>
          <li><code class="text-[0.85em] bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">POST /events</code> — create an event (write token; required: calendarId, summary, startsAt, endsAt)</li>
          <li><code class="text-[0.85em] bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">PATCH /events/{id} · DELETE /events/{id}</code> — update / delete an event (write token; delete is soft — restore with POST /events/{id}/restore)</li>
          <li><code class="text-[0.85em] bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">POST /calendars/{id}/import/preview · POST /calendars/{id}/import</code> — preview / import ICS (write token; JSON body {"text": "the whole .ics text"}, max 8 MB, same dedupe rules as the web import)</li>
          <li><code class="text-[0.85em] bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">GET /calendars/{id}/export.ics</code> — download a whole calendar as an .ics file (use this for backups)</li>
          <li><code class="text-[0.85em] bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">GET /calendars/{id}/subscriptions · POST</code> — list / add external ICS subscriptions (adding needs a write token); POST /calendars/{id}/subscriptions/{subId}/refresh refreshes now; DELETE removes one</li>
          <li><code class="text-[0.85em] bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">GET /search?q=keyword</code> — search events</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="font-medium text-slate-800 mb-1.5">curl examples</p>
        <pre class="mt-2 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-3 text-xs leading-relaxed">curl -H "Authorization: Bearer <redacted>" "<%= baseUrl %>/api/v1/calendars"
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer <redacted>" "<%= baseUrl %>/api/v1/events?from=2026-01-05T00:00:00+11:00&amp;to=2026-01-12T00:00:00+11:00"
curl -X POST "<%= baseUrl %>/api/v1/events" -H "Authorization: Bearer <redacted>" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"calendarId":"&lt;calendar-id&gt;","summary":"Report","startsAt":"2026-01-05T14:00:00+11:00","endsAt":"2026-01-05T15:00:00+11:00"}'</pre>
        <p class="font-medium text-slate-800 mb-1.5 mt-3">Error codes & limits</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 mb-3">
          <li><code class="text-[0.85em] bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">401 invalid_token</code> — wrong, revoked or expired token, the API is disabled, or the account is suspended (see the checklist in the item above)</li>
          <li><code class="text-[0.85em] bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">403 token_is_read_only</code> — a read-only token tried to write; read-only tokens can only GET</li>
          <li><code class="text-[0.85em] bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">400 invalid_body / bad_query / ends_before_starts</code> — malformed body or parameters (missing required fields, missing from/to, end before start)</li>
          <li><code class="text-[0.85em] bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">404 not_found / calendar_not_found</code> — doesn't exist, or isn't yours (other people's calendars and events always look nonexistent)</li>
          <li><code class="text-[0.85em] bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">413 file_too_large / 422 import_failed</code> — import over 8 MB / the ICS content couldn't be parsed</li>
          <li><code class="text-[0.85em] bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">429 too_many_requests</code> — site-wide rate limit hit (per IP, 120 per minute by default, operator-adjustable); wait a minute and retry</li>
        </ul>
        <p>A token can only reach your own calendars. Usage (last used time, source IP, total call count) is shown next to each token under Settings → Devices → API tokens — revoke tokens you no longer use.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="group">
      <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 py-4 cursor-pointer select-none list-none font-medium text-slate-800 group-hover:text-brand-700">
        <span>Registration &amp; verification emails</span>
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-slate-400 shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M5.23 7.21a.75.75 0 011.06.02L10 11.17l3.71-3.94a.75.75 0 111.08 1.04l-4.25 4.5a.75.75 0 01-1.08 0l-4.25-4.5a.75.75 0 01.02-1.06z" clip-rule="evenodd"/></svg>
      </summary>
      <div class="pb-5 text-sm text-slate-600">
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>After you register, enter the verification code sent to your email to finish setting up the account.</li>
          <li>No email? Check the spam folder and give it a few minutes. Still nothing — use the resend option on the verification page.</li>
          <li>If the code has expired, request a fresh one instead of retrying the old code.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="group">
      <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 py-4 cursor-pointer select-none list-none font-medium text-slate-800 group-hover:text-brand-700">
        <span>What an error code means</span>
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-slate-400 shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M5.23 7.21a.75.75 0 011.06.02L10 11.17l3.71-3.94a.75.75 0 111.08 1.04l-4.25 4.5a.75.75 0 01-1.08 0l-4.25-4.5a.75.75 0 01.02-1.06z" clip-rule="evenodd"/></svg>
      </summary>
      <div class="pb-5 text-sm text-slate-600">
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li><code class="text-[0.85em] bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">401 invalid_token</code> — the token is wrong, revoked or expired, the API is switched off, or the account is suspended. Work through the API token entry above.</li>
          <li><code class="text-[0.85em] bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">403 token_is_read_only</code> — the token is read-only but the tool tried to write. Create a read &amp; write token, or let the tool only read.</li>
          <li><code class="text-[0.85em] bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">400</code> — something in the request is off (for example a missing start or end time). Check the tool's field mapping.</li>
          <li><code class="text-[0.85em] bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">404</code> — the calendar or event doesn't exist, or it isn't yours. <code class="text-[0.85em] bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">429</code> — too many requests; wait a bit and retry. <code class="text-[0.85em] bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">5xx</code> — a server-side problem; try again later.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="group">
      <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 py-4 cursor-pointer select-none list-none font-medium text-slate-800 group-hover:text-brand-700">
        <span>Before asking for help: what to include</span>
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-slate-400 shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M5.23 7.21a.75.75 0 011.06.02L10 11.17l3.71-3.94a.75.75 0 111.08 1.04l-4.25 4.5a.75.75 0 01-1.08 0l-4.25-4.5a.75.75 0 01.02-1.06z" clip-rule="evenodd"/></svg>
      </summary>
      <div class="pb-5 text-sm text-slate-600">
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>The server version — open <code class="text-[0.85em] bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">/health</code> in your browser and copy the version shown. Also note your client and its version, your browser, and the time and timezone when it happened.</li>
          <li>What you did, step by step, and what you expected to happen instead.</li>
          <li>Before posting anywhere public, remove passwords, full tokens and email addresses from screenshots and logs.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </details>

<details class="group">
      <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 py-4 cursor-pointer select-none list-none font-medium text-slate-800 group-hover:text-brand-700">
        <span>Close account / delete all data</span>
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-slate-400 shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M5.23 7.21a.75.75 0 011.06.02L10 11.17l3.71-3.94a.75.75 0 111.08 1.04l-4.25 4.5a.75.75 0 01-1.08 0l-4.25-4.5a.75.75 0 01.02-1.06z" clip-rule="evenodd"/></svg>
      </summary>
      <div class="pb-5 text-sm text-slate-600">
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>On the web or in the app: Settings → Account → Danger Zone → "Delete Account". <strong class="font-semibold text-slate-900">This action is irreversible</strong> and clears all your calendars, events, invitations, and device bindings.</li>
          <li>If you want to back up before deleting, export an .ics file to your local device before deletion.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </details>

  </div>

  <!-- Contact channels -->
  <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-1">Still not resolved?</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mb-4">Choose the entry point that matches the type of issue to get an answer fastest.</p>

  <div class="divide-y divide-slate-200 border-y border-slate-200 mb-10">
    <!-- Operator -->
    <div class="grid gap-1 sm:grid-cols-[210px_1fr] sm:gap-8 py-5">
      <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900">Account / data / server</h3>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 max-w-2xl">Locked accounts, data recovery, maintenance windows, and the like. All data resides on the <strong class="font-medium text-slate-700">site operator's</strong> server, so please contact the operator (contact details in the footer).</p>
    </div>
    <!-- GitHub -->
    <div class="grid gap-1 sm:grid-cols-[210px_1fr] sm:gap-8 py-5">
      <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900">App / software bug</h3>
      <div>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 max-w-2xl">Frontend / app / server-side bugs, feature suggestions, and open-source collaboration.</p>
        <div class="mt-2 flex flex-col gap-1 text-sm">
          <a href="https://github.com/wuha-like-sleep/by-wave-calendar/issues" class="text-brand-700 hover:underline font-medium">Submit an Issue ↗</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/wuha-like-sleep/by-wave-calendar/discussions" class="text-brand-700 hover:underline">Discussions ↗</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <!-- Email -->
    <div class="grid gap-1 sm:grid-cols-[210px_1fr] sm:gap-8 py-5">
      <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900">Business / media / general</h3>
      <div>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 max-w-2xl">Enterprise deployment inquiries, partnerships, and general questions.</p>
        <a href="mailto:info@by-wave.com" class="mt-2 inline-block text-sm text-brand-700 hover:underline font-mono break-all">info@by-wave.com</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Response times -->
  <div>
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 text-sm mb-2.5">Expected response times</h3>
    <ul class="text-sm text-slate-600 space-y-1.5">
      <li><strong class="font-medium text-slate-800">GitHub Issues</strong> — usually a reply within 1–7 days; for urgent security issues, please email us as well.</li>
      <li><strong class="font-medium text-slate-800">Email</strong> — 1–3 business days (noting the type in the subject line, such as "[Bug] iOS week view…" or "[Business] Enterprise deployment", helps us triage faster).</li>
      <li><strong class="font-medium text-slate-800">Site account issues</strong> — depends on the site operator, who usually states their expected response time on the homepage / login page.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-3">This is an open-source, self-hosted project maintained by volunteers, with no 24/7 support — thank you for understanding.</p>
  </div>

</div>
